{
  "homepage": "https://github.com/bh679/dungeon-train-mc",
  "1.21.1": {
    "0.1104.0": "**New Feature \u00d76 \u00b7 Bug Fix \u00d75 \u00b7 Editor \u00d75 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d72 \u00b7 Train \u00d72 \u00b7 Menus & UI \u00d72 \u00b7 Balance \u00d72 \u00b7 Performance \u00d71 \u00b7 Multiplayer \u00d71 \u00b7 Community \u00d71 \u00b7 World \u00d71 \u00b7 Loot \u00d71 \u00b7 Books \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1104.0\n\n**Narrative tab shortcut**\n\nThe creative inventory's left edge now has a shortcut to the Dungeon Train narrative tab.\n\n### 0.1103.0\n\n**Longer carriages**\n\nSome carriages on the train are now much longer.\n\n### 0.1102.0\n\n**Your own library turns up when you've written something**\n\nA dimensional carriage is more likely to open onto a library of your own books after you've written one.\n\n### 0.1101.0\n\n**Bookshelves trade four for an emerald**\n\nVillagers now give one emerald's worth for every four bookshelves.\n\n### 0.1100.0\n\n**Tidier creative inventory**\n\nThe creative inventory now keeps to the vanilla and Dungeon Train tabs, and the mod block tabs and their search entries can be switched back on from Options, Dungeon Train, Editor.\n\n### 0.1099.0\n\n**See what others are up to**\n\nYou can now see what the players riding with you are doing.\n\n### 0.1098.0\n\n**Main menu tidy-up**\n\nSmall main menu tidy-up.\n\n### 0.1097.0\n\n**Carriage group builds keep their variants and loot**\n\nCarriage group builds made in the Train Builder now keep their block variants and chest loot when saved and shared.\n\n### 0.1096.0\n\n**Editor Menus setting stays put**\n\nThe editor's Editor Menus setting now stays as you left it when you test a carriage.\n\n### 0.1095.0\n\n**Tidier joins between terrain styles**\n\nWith the optional border-blending setting on, trees and other features now stay with their own terrain where two styles meet.\n\n### 0.1094.0\n\n**Leaving a world**\n\nLeaving a world no longer crashes the game now and then.",
    "0.1093.0": "**New Feature \u00d75 \u00b7 Editor \u00d73 \u00b7 Bug Fix \u00d72 \u00b7 Menus & UI \u00d72 \u00b7 Multiplayer \u00d71 \u00b7 Community \u00d71 \u00b7 Translations \u00d71 \u00b7 World \u00d71 \u00b7 Mobs \u00d71 \u00b7 Behind the Scenes \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1093.0\n\n**Supported mods**\n\nInternal changes to how supported mods are handled, to meet CurseForge's requirements.\n\n### 0.1092.0\n\n**Things that grow**\n\nVines, glow berries, ladders, bamboo, dripstone and more can now grow into longer columns in your builds, and the overgrown tunnels hang a little lower.\n\n### 0.1091.0\n\n**Shift exits on the pause menu, on servers too**\n\nHolding Shift on the pause menu now reveals the Exit to Title and Quit Game buttons on a server as well, with Disconnect still there when Shift is up.\n\n### 0.1089.0\n\n**An ode to Monty Python**\n\nSomething out there may now introduce itself with a name that Monty Python fans will recognise.\n\n### 0.1088.0\n\n**Build editor messages in your language**\n\nThe build editor's quick messages above the hotbar now speak your language.\n\n### 0.1087.0\n\n**Submitted builds show their picture**\n\nBuilds submitted for review from the editor now arrive with their picture, whole rooms included.\n\n### 0.1086.0\n\n**Bug reports from /bug and /feedback get an answer**\n\nSending a bug report with /bug or /feedback now replies in chat with what might help.",
    "0.1085.0": "**New Feature \u00d75 \u00b7 Menus & UI \u00d73 \u00b7 Translations \u00d72 \u00b7 Community \u00d71 \u00b7 Mobs \u00d71 \u00b7 Loot \u00d71 \u00b7 Books \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1084.0\n\n**See your translation where it appears**\n\nTranslators can now preview their text in place \u2014 on a book page, a button, a tooltip, the death screen, in chat and more \u2014 before saving.\n\n### 0.1083.0\n\n**Your bug reports get an answer**\n\nReport a bug after a fall and the train now tells you whether help is already on the way.\n\n### 0.1082.0\n\n**Know who's speaking**\n\nTranslators can see more info about the characters they're translating for.\n\n### 0.1081.0\n\n**Echoes leave their mark**\n\nGear an echo leaves behind now remembers who it belonged to.\n\n### 0.1077.0\n\n**Leaderboard eras and Ancient Records**\n\nThe one-life leaderboards now belong to eras. When a balancing release changes what a good run is, the boards are retired and a fresh set opens for the new version; each calendar year gets its own boards too. Nothing is lost: every retired board is kept for good, and The Tallyman's books about them keep turning up in loot as Ancient Records, naming the game versions their numbers came from. Players still on an older version keep scoring on their own era's boards.\n\n- One-life boards (distance, carriages, time aboard, chests, echoes, friends, pacifist and no-chest runs) reset per game version; all-lives totals and contribution boards stay all-time.\n- Retired boards stay readable and circulate as Ancient Records books: about one loot book in forty, and one per retired era on the Stat Room's shelves. The server setting retiredLeaderboardBooks turns them off.\n- Each year has its own one-life boards alongside the version boards.",
    "0.1080.0": "**Bug Fix \u00d76 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d76 \u00b7 World \u00d76 \u00b7 New Feature \u00d75 \u00b7 Performance \u00d74 \u00b7 Train \u00d73 \u00b7 Behind the Scenes \u00d73 \u00b7 Community \u00d72 \u00b7 Menus & UI \u00d72 \u00b7 New Content \u00d71 \u00b7 Editor \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1080.0\n\n**Trash slot won't keep holding items when menu closes**\n\nAnything still sitting in the trash slot that hasn't been intentionally deleted now comes back to you when you close your inventory.\n\n### 0.1079.0\n\n**Feedback shows your version**\n\nFeedback you send from the game now says which version of Dungeon Train you were playing.\n\n### 0.1078.0\n\n**Cargo carriages**\n\nCargo carriages turn up in more shapes along the line.\n\n### 0.1077.0\n\n**Islands arrive whole**\n\nFloating scenery no longer shows up as bare squares when you arrive somewhere in a hurry, and the world builds itself a little faster there.\n\n### 0.1076.0\n\n**Steadier train**\n\nThe train no longer jumps.\n\n### 0.1075.0\n\n**Lighter on memory after busy stretches**\n\nThe game now lets go of memory it no longer needs once you've ridden on past the world's busiest stretches.\n\n### 0.1073.0\n\n**Plants stay rooted**\n\nPlants along the line now only grow where they can stand.\n\n**No more hard edges**\n\nSome scenery now carries on past where it used to stop.\n\n### 0.1071.0\n\n**The train gets going again after a visit to a tall dimensional carriage**\n\nStepping back onto the train after exploring one of the taller dimensional carriages now sets it rolling again straight away.\n\n### 0.1070.0\n\n**Lighter world generation**\n\nNew land around the train now takes a little less work to generate.\n\n### 0.1069.0\n\n**Support logs say whether Sable Pathfinder is installed**\n\nYour log now notes at world load whether the Sable Pathfinder companion is installed, so help requests can be answered faster.\n\n### 0.1068.0\n\n**A companion mod now installs on its own on CurseForge**\n\nOne more small companion mod now installs alongside Dungeon Train on CurseForge; nothing changes in-game.\n\n### 0.1067.0\n\n**Steadier world loading**\n\nDungeon Train worlds now load more reliably alongside other terrain mods.\n\n### 0.1066.0\n\n**Submitted builds get announced**\n\nSubmitting a build for review now shares it, picture and all, with the community on Discord.\n\n### 0.1065.0\n\n**Faster world start-up**\n\nWorlds now finish loading sooner.\n\n### 0.1064.0\n\n**Other worlds left alone**\n\nYour other worlds now behave as they normally would.\n\n### 0.1063.0\n\n**Fresher companion mods in the modpack**\n\nThe modpack now installs the newest versions of its companion mods.",
    "0.1062.0": "**World \u00d72 \u00b7 New Feature \u00d71 \u00b7 Bug Fix \u00d71 \u00b7 Performance \u00d71 \u00b7 Editor \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1062.0\n\n**Blended landscapes feel of a piece**\n\nWhere two landscapes blend into each other, the air and the creatures now match the ground beneath your feet.\n\n### 0.1061.0\n\n**Smoother building generation**\n\nBig ruined buildings along the line now appear with less of a hitch.\n\n### 0.1060.0\n\n**Carriage contents come in three sizes**\n\nThe editor can now build carriage contents at Room, Half and Full size, and each carriage only takes contents of its own size.",
    "0.1059.0": "**New Feature \u00d71 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d71 \u00b7 World \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1059.0\n\n**Backported from the future**\n\nA little of the future has been backported into the present past \u2014 new biomes, mobs and blocks are waiting to be found.",
    "0.1058.0": "**New Feature \u00d73 \u00b7 Editor \u00d72 \u00b7 World \u00d71 \u00b7 Menus & UI \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1058.0\n\n**Tunnels keep their look**\n\nTunnels now hold one style for longer stretches, and blend more cleanly as the world grows darker.\n\n### 0.1056.0\n\n**Test from the editor with Ctrl/Cmd+R**\n\nCtrl/Cmd+R in the editor now takes you straight into testing what you're building.\n\n**Reseeding a test carriage keeps your view**\n\nReseeding a test carriage now leaves you where you were from a little further away.",
    "0.1055.0": "**New Feature \u00d77 \u00b7 Editor \u00d77 \u00b7 World \u00d72 \u00b7 Bug Fix \u00d71 \u00b7 Community \u00d71 \u00b7 Train \u00d71 \u00b7 Loot \u00d71 \u00b7 Menus & UI \u00d71 \u00b7 Balance \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1055.0\n\n**Community item trade values**\n\nWhat items trade for with villagers can now be suggested and voted on by the community at brennan.games/dungeontrain/items.\n\n### 0.1054.0\n\n**Blocks page in the editor**\n\nThe X editor can now show every block in a build and swap any of them for the one in your hand.\n\n### 0.1053.0\n\n**Overworld dimensional carriages find their ground**\n\nOverworld dimensional carriages, and testing them from the editor, now reliably find somewhere to stand.\n\n### 0.1052.0\n\n**Two dimensional carriage styles go by simpler names in the editor**\n\nTwo dimensional carriage styles now go by simpler names in the editor, and anything built under the old names carries on as before.\n\n### 0.1051.0\n\n**Tunnel styles have their places**\n\nEach tunnel style now turns up only on the stretches of the journey it belongs to.\n\n### 0.1050.0\n\n**Editor arrivals take flight**\n\nJumping to a template in the editor no longer leaves you falling when there's nothing to stand on.\n\n### 0.1049.0\n\n**Tunnels keep one look**\n\nEach tunnel now keeps one look from entrance to exit, and there are new ones to ride through \u2014 some built by Pumpkin_P_Patch.\n\n### 0.1048.0\n\n**Train Editor: new rooms start switched off**\n\nIn the Train Editor, a newly made carriage room now starts switched off in every carriage's Contents list, and only appears once you switch it on.",
    "0.1047.0": "**Bug Fix \u00d71 \u00b7 Train \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1047.0\n\n**Dimensional carriages on the way back**\n\nRiding the train backwards, dimensional carriages now turn up no more often than they do going forwards.",
    "0.1046.0": "**Editor \u00d79 \u00b7 New Feature \u00d77 \u00b7 Menus & UI \u00d73 \u00b7 Bug Fix \u00d72 \u00b7 Community \u00d71 \u00b7 Train \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1046.0\n\n**Fences that join up your way**\n\nStage fences and walls now join up, and builders can pick exactly how any fence or wall connects.\n\n### 0.1045.0\n\n**Test the Carriage for track pieces**\n\nTrack, pillar, stairs and tunnel templates can now be tested from the editor, with a carriage standing right where the piece is.\n\n### 0.1044.0\n\n**Tunnel templates show the train's path**\n\nTunnel templates in the editor now show where the train will pass, and anything built in its way glows red.\n\n### 0.1043.0\n\n**Paintings stay on the wall**\n\nPaintings in carriages now stay hanging where they were placed, on the train and in Test the Carriage.\n\n### 0.1042.0\n\n**Open template files**\n\nThe editor can now take you straight to where a template's files are saved.\n\n### 0.1041.0\n\n**Stage blocks come in colour**\n\nBuilders can now place terracotta, concrete, stained glass and glazed terracotta that take on each stage's own colours.\n\n### 0.1040.0\n\n**Saved whole rooms reach My Builds**\n\nWhole rooms you save in the editor now show up in My Builds.\n\n### 0.1039.0\n\n**Stage Blocks get their own creative tab**\n\nStage blocks now sit in their own tab along the side of the creative inventory, styled like the rest.\n\n### 0.1038.0\n\n**Stage blocks show which way is up**\n\nStage blocks in the editor now mark their top and bottom, with a small arrow on each side pointing up.",
    "0.1037.0": "**New Feature \u00d73 \u00b7 Editor \u00d73 \u00b7 Bug Fix \u00d72 \u00b7 World \u00d71 \u00b7 Mobs \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1037.0\n\n**Test mode reminder**\n\nBuilding inside a carriage you're testing now reminds you that none of it will be kept.\n\n### 0.1036.0\n\n**Improvement to structure worldgen**\n\nWhere two Lost City buildings stand on the same spot, both now keep their walls and floors.\n\n### 0.1035.0\n\n**Test the Carriage starts on a flatbed**\n\nTesting a carriage now starts you on a flatbed, looking at two rolls of it.\n\n### 0.1034.0\n\n**Reseed leaves you where you are**\n\nReseeding a test carriage now leaves you where you were standing, as long as you're close by.\n\n### 0.1033.0\n\n**Something in the grass**\n\nNot every rabbit is as harmless as it looks.",
    "0.1032.0": "**World \u00d74 \u00b7 New Feature \u00d73 \u00b7 Mobs \u00d72 \u00b7 Performance \u00d71 \u00b7 Loot \u00d71 \u00b7 Behind the Scenes \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1032.0\n\n**New ruins along the line**\n\nMore ruined buildings can be found along the way, each a little different every time you pass one.\n\n### 0.1031.0\n\n**Lost City Terrain Fit is now its own mod**\n\nThe terrain-fitting for ruined-city buildings has moved into its own mod, Lost City Terrain Fit, which comes bundled with Dungeon Train. Nothing extra to install.\n\n### 0.1030.0\n\n**Shorter stretches along the line**\n\nSeveral stretches of the line are now shorter, and the journey moves between some of them more smoothly.\n\n### 0.1029.0\n\n**More caves**\n\nMore caves. The mountains the line climbs through are no longer solid rock \u2014 big open caves now run through them, and the track carries you straight through.\n\n### 0.1028.0\n\n**Faster terrain generation**\n\nNew terrain around the train now takes less server work to generate. The world itself is unchanged.",
    "0.1027.0": "**Bug Fix \u00d71 \u00b7 Performance \u00d71 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d71 \u00b7 Train \u00d71 \u00b7 World \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1027.0\n\n**Smoother ticks with Distant Horizons**\n\nDistant Horizons now generates its distant terrain more gently, so the train and the world keep ticking smoothly on smaller CPUs while it works in the background.\n\n### 0.1026.0\n\n**Returning from the End puts you back on your train**\n\nComing back through the End's exit portal now lands you on the train you left.",
    "0.1025.0": "**Performance \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1025.0\n\n**No more freezes when the train runs into new land**\n\nThe game could freeze for a fraction of a second when the train ran into land that was still being generated, while it waited for that ground to finish. It now carries on and deals with that stretch a moment later, once it's ready.\n\n- Fewer hitches when riding fast into unexplored terrain\n- The train still breaks blocks in its path and pushes water aside as before",
    "0.1024.0": "**Performance \u00d72 \u00b7 New Feature \u00d71 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d71 \u00b7 Menus & UI \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1024.0\n\n**Less dev logging**\n\nLess dev logs.\n\n### 0.1023.0\n\n**A heads-up when Minecraft is short on memory**\n\nIf your launcher gives Minecraft too little memory, the game can stutter and freeze as it runs out. Dungeon Train now tells you when that's the case and shows you how to fix it in your launcher.\n\n- A notice on the title screen when Minecraft has under 5 GB of memory and your computer has more to give\n- \"How to do it\" opens a step-by-step guide for your launcher: CurseForge, Modrinth App, the Minecraft Launcher, Prism, MultiMC or ATLauncher\n- The modpack now recommends 6 GB of memory\n- Turn it off with \"Don't show again\", or in Options > Dungeon Train > Low Memory Warning",
    "0.1022.0": "**Bug Fix \u00d72 \u00b7 Community \u00d71 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d71 \u00b7 Books \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1022.0\n\n**Community books keep their author's layout**\n\nCommunity books now appear exactly as their author laid them out \u2014 indentation, blank lines and word art are preserved, and pages stay where they were written instead of spilling onto extra pages.\n\n- Word art and centred text in found books are no longer flattened\n- Blank spacer lines survive, so signatures and page breaks stay where the author put them\n\n### 0.1021.0\n\n**Quick play no longer stops at the title screen when a Distant Horizons update is pending**\n\nLaunching straight into a server or world (Minecraft's quick play) used to stall on the title screen whenever Distant Horizons had an update to offer, because the mod hid that prompt by opening a fresh title screen. The join now goes ahead as intended.\n\n- The Distant Horizons update prompt is still kept out of the way for the modpack's pinned build; nothing changes for other Distant Horizons versions.",
    "0.1020.0": "**Performance \u00d73 \u00b7 World \u00d73 \u00b7 New Feature \u00d72 \u00b7 Bug Fix \u00d72 \u00b7 Train \u00d72 \u00b7 Behind the Scenes \u00d72 \u00b7 Editor \u00d71 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1020.0\n\n**More useful lag reports**\n\nBehind the scenes: lag reports now record what else was slowing the game down besides the train, such as memory clean-up pauses, waiting on terrain to load, and how many creatures are riding along. Nothing changes in play.\n\n- Lag reports can now tell apart memory pauses, terrain loading and busy carriages\n\n### 0.1019.0\n\n**No more freezes when water or lava flows into terrain that is still generating**\n\nWhen water or lava reached the edge of terrain that had not finished generating, the server used to stop everything and build that terrain on the spot \u2014 a multi-second freeze, sometimes chained several times over. The check for what the two fluids should do when they meet now waits until the terrain is ready, then runs as normal, so obsidian and cobblestone still form and the train keeps moving.\n\n- Multi-second freezes at the edge of freshly generated terrain are gone\n- Lava and water still turn to obsidian, cobblestone and basalt as before, just a moment later at chunk edges\n\n### 0.1018.0\n\n**Smoother ticks when new carriages join the train**\n\nEach time the train grew by a group of carriages, the physics engine was told about every single block as it was placed \u2014 thousands of tiny collision updates in one tick, which showed up as a stutter right after each new group appeared. The train now builds a whole group first and hands the physics engine each finished chunk section once, so joining carriages cost a fraction of what they did. Mining or placing blocks on a carriage still updates collision immediately.\n\n- Far fewer physics collision updates when a group of carriages is added\n- New performance counters in the lag log so the remaining cost is visible\n\n### 0.1017.0\n\n**Fewer ruins**\n\nRuins turn up a little less often along the line.\n\n### 0.1016.0\n\n**No more \"non-existent sub-level\" errors while riding**\n\nRiding the train no longer fills your log with \"Received a sub-level movement packet for a non-existent sub-level\" errors. New carriages now reach your game in the right order, so their first movement update never arrives before the carriage itself.\n\n### 0.1015.0\n\n**Smoother streaming into a later phase's terrain**\n\nEntering one of the later phases could freeze the game for several seconds at a time: the pass that clears stray overworld trees and flowers from the freshly generated terrain ran on the main server thread for every new chunk, and the train generates about a chunk a second. That pass now runs on the world-generation workers, skips terrain that has nothing to clear, and only the handful of block removals stays on the main thread. The generated world is unchanged.\n\n- No more multi-second freezes while new terrain streams in around the transition into a later phase\n- Same terrain and vegetation as before \u2014 only where the work runs changed\n- A server config setting can restore the old in-line pass if ever needed\n\n### 0.1014.0\n\n**Your additions to the train break off when they hit things**\n\nBlocks you build onto the train are no longer as tough as the train itself. When something you've added hits a hillside, a tunnel wall or another moving contraption, it breaks off and drops as items, and whatever it hit stays standing. The train's own carriages still plough through terrain exactly as before.\n\n- Blocks you place on the train break off, and drop as items, when they hit terrain or another physics object\n- Chests you've added spill their contents when they break off\n- The train's own blocks are unchanged: they never break and still carve through terrain\n\n### 0.1013.0\n\n**Work-in-progress carriage builds**\n\nBehind the scenes: a new stairway room and carriage group, and a reworked cave room, are saved for later. None of them appear on the train yet.\n\n- Builds saved for a future update; nothing changes in play",
    "0.1012.0": "**New Feature \u00d75 \u00b7 Bug Fix \u00d74 \u00b7 World \u00d74 \u00b7 Mobs \u00d73 \u00b7 Performance \u00d72 \u00b7 Editor \u00d71 \u00b7 Community \u00d71 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d71 \u00b7 Loot \u00d71 \u00b7 Balance \u00d71 \u00b7 Behind the Scenes \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1012.0\n\n**New worlds load about twice as fast**\n\nCreating a new world now takes about half as long. The game no longer builds large structures it was only going to throw away, and the biggest ones further down the line are loaded quietly in the background before the train gets there, so arriving doesn't hitch.\n\n- New worlds open in roughly half the time\n- Large structures load in the background ahead of the train instead of all at once when you reach them\n- Early on, each world now draws from its own smaller mix of structures, so every world looks a little different\n- Using /locate no longer freezes the server when searching for some structures\n\n### 0.1011.0\n\n**Keep an eye on the sky**\n\nSomething strange stirs in one of the later stretches of the line. Ride far enough and you might notice it.\n\n### 0.1010.0\n\n**Friends who travel together now dress for it**\n\nWhen a player mob boards the train with a friend in tow, that friend now arrives kitted out for how far you've come, and it counts as one of the train's own passengers.\n\n- The friend now rolls its own armour and weapon for your current difficulty, instead of showing up empty-handed beside its fully geared partner\n- The friend is no longer cleared away when it wanders into a dimensional carriage\n\n### 0.1009.0\n\n**Internal improvements**\n\nBehind-the-scenes maintenance work. Nothing to see or do differently in game.\n\n### 0.1008.0\n\n**Small change to clocks and compasses**\n\nSmall change to clocks and compasses.\n\n### 0.1007.0\n\n**Fewer ruins early on**\n\nThe ruins scattered along an early stretch of the line now turn up less often \u2014 about 70% as many as before.\n\n### 0.1006.0\n\n**A PlayerMob's travelling friend has a name too**\n\nWhen two PlayerMobs board the train together as friends, the second one used to walk around with no name above its head. Both now get a name, the same way a PlayerMob always has.\n\n- Friends who board as an echo pair still read \"Echo of \u2026\", unchanged\n\n### 0.1005.0\n\n**Generosity in drifting carriages is remembered**\n\nLeaving something good in a drifting carriage's chest for the next traveller now counts in your favour: the echo you leave behind comes back a little friendlier. The better the gift, the more it counts.\n\n- Items you leave in storage in someone else's drifting carriage make your echo friendlier, scaled by what they're worth\n- Taking something out and putting it back doesn't count twice\n\n### 0.1004.0\n\n**Joining no longer freezes the game, and stepping off the train stays smooth**\n\nThree causes of lag are gone: a freeze of up to a minute when joining a world on hilly ground, a freeze when water flowed near a carriage at the edge of loaded land, and a steady slowdown that built up whenever you were away from the train, which made picking up items and the train's own movement feel late. Ticks now stay fast whether you are aboard or off exploring.\n\n- Joining a world no longer stalls while the game looks for a spot to start the intro shot\n- Blocks changing on a carriage next to unloaded land no longer freeze the server\n- Wandering away from the train no longer makes the game grind: the carriages you left behind stay cheap to simulate\n- New server option spawnSearchSyncGen (off by default) brings back the old, wider spawn search if you want it\n\n### 0.1003.0\n\n**Stage Leaves block for builders**\n\nA new Stage Leaves block becomes the leaves that match each stage's wood, and Test the Carriage now shows stage blocks as they will look on the train.\n\n### 0.1002.0\n\n**Potions are worth emeralds**\n\nVillagers now pay real emeralds for potions, and stronger brews are worth more.\n\n- Potions with an effect now trade for emeralds\n- More potent, longer-lasting and lingering potions fetch a better price\n- Water bottles and other effect-less brews are unchanged",
    "0.1001.0": "**New Feature \u00d72 \u00b7 Editor \u00d71 \u00b7 Community \u00d71 \u00b7 Train \u00d71 \u00b7 World \u00d71**\n\n### 0.1001.0\n\n**Dimensional carriages drift**\n\nDimensional carriages now drift the way carriages do. Build in one and your work is carried on down the line, with your name and changes travelling on.\n\n- One in fifteen sealed (Bedrock Lock) dimensional carriages drifts: it uploads when edited and can arrive as another traveller's copy\n- Builders are credited on entry, just like a drifting carriage\n- New per-room Drift setting in the editor panel and /dt editor portals <room> drift\n\n### 0.1000.0\n\n**A quicker reassembly**\n\nThe stretch where the world stitches itself back together is now a little shorter, so you're back on solid ground sooner.\n\n- The reassembling stretch is about a sixth shorter; everything after it arrives sooner",
    "0.999.0": "**New Feature \u00d72 \u00b7 Community \u00d71 \u00b7 Advancements \u00d71**\n\n### 0.999.0\n\n**The Secrete Menu**\n\n\u2026\n\n### 0.998.0\n\n**Drifting carriage improvements**\n\nDrifting carriages hold on to more of what their builders leave behind.",
    "0.998.0": "**New Feature \u00d74 \u00b7 World \u00d72 \u00b7 Advancements \u00d72 \u00b7 Bug Fix \u00d71 \u00b7 Editor \u00d71 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d71**\n\n### 0.998.0\n\n**The journey takes a new route**\n\nThe line now runs through its landscapes in a different order, so some of the places you used to reach late in a run come sooner, and others come later.\n\n- The stretches of the journey have been reshuffled.\n- One stretch now blends gradually into the next instead of stopping at a hard edge.\n- Structures along the line now sit into the land: the ground climbs over and into them, water flows through them where they stand in it, and they appear in every kind of terrain.\n- They gather gradually rather than all at once, and a few now turn up earlier in the journey.\n\n### 0.997.0\n\n**Advancements reveal one step at a time**\n\nThe advancements screen now shows only what you've earned plus the next step ahead \u2014 everything further along stays hidden until you reach it.\n\n### 0.996.0\n\n**Faulthurst's Favourite hint in every language**\n\nFaulthurst's Favourite now gives a hint before you earn it in every language, not just English.\n\n**Effortless Building follows the editor's mirror, and whole rooms can be test-driven**\n\nIn the train editor, Effortless Building now respects a template's mirror settings. Lines, walls, cubes and breaks you make with it appear on the mirrored side too, and its ghost preview shows both halves before you place. One Ctrl+Z undoes both halves. Test the Carriage now works on whole rooms and whole groups, so you can walk through them before they ride the train.\n\n- Effortless Building places and breaks are mirrored in mirror-enabled templates, including its own undo and redo\n- The Effortless Building preview shows the mirrored half, even when you build into a template from outside it\n- Test the Carriage works for whole rooms and whole groups, with Reseed and Back\n- Whole groups can now be set as rare as one in every 1000 groups\n\n**New ground behind you**\n\nHead back along the train past where you boarded and the journey now carries on behind you, in its own order. But the train has to take you there: only ground you cover walking back along the train brings the next stretch closer, while jumping off or flying ahead just pushes it further away.\n\n- Heading back past where you boarded now leads into new stretches\n- Only distance covered on the train counts; getting off or flying ahead doesn't bring you closer\n- Smoother edges where the strangest stretch gives way to ordinary land",
    "0.995.0": "**New Feature \u00d71 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d71 \u00b7 World \u00d71 \u00b7 Behind the Scenes \u00d71**\n\n### 0.995.0\n\n**Some things hold together until you touch them**\n\nLoose sand and gravel out in the stranger stretches of the journey no longer crumble away the moment you arrive. They hang where they were built, just like sand over a cave, until you disturb them.\n\n- Loose blocks stay put until you mine or build next to them.\n\n**CurseForge installs three companion mods alongside Dungeon Train**\n\nOn CurseForge, the OBS/Streamlabs check behind the Videos tab, the zapret/GoodbyeDPI check behind the connection warning, and one more small companion mod now install as their own mods next to Dungeon Train instead of living inside it. Nothing changes in-game, and Modrinth and manual installs keep them built in.\n\n- The CurseForge app installs them for you automatically\n- Modrinth and manual installs are unchanged",
    "0.994.0": "**New Feature \u00d77 \u00b7 Bug Fix \u00d73 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d73 \u00b7 World \u00d72 \u00b7 Menus & UI \u00d72 \u00b7 Translations \u00d71 \u00b7 Train \u00d71 \u00b7 Mobs \u00d71 \u00b7 Loot \u00d71 \u00b7 Balance \u00d71**\n\n### 0.994.0\n\n**Dimensional carriages stay clean on later visits**\n\nDeep into a run, a dimensional carriage could appear with bedrock where its void should be, and walking in could bounce you straight back onto the train with \"This room lost its train\". Each carriage now gets its own space again.\n\n- Void rooms stay void \u2014 no stray bedrock from rooms you passed long ago\n- No more being put back on the train the moment you step into a room\n\n### 0.993.0\n\n**Free Play explained the same way everywhere**\n\nEvery screen that mentions Free Play now explains it with the same words: advancements and stats won't be saved. Where you still have a choice to make, it adds that Free Play is a safe space to use hacks and cheats.\n\n- The Free Play explanation now reads the same in chat, tooltips, menus and prompts\n- Updated Free Play translations in every supported language\n\n### 0.992.0\n\n**No more holes in the scenery**\n\nAlong some of the stranger stretches of the line, the scenery beside the track now fills in first, instead of leaving square holes of empty sky for a while \u2014 or for good, if you moved on too quickly.\n\n- Scenery closest to you fills in first\n- No more square gaps left behind when the server is busy\n\n### 0.991.0\n\n**Bookshelves and honey blocks trade for 1 emerald**\n\nVillagers now give 1 emerald for a bookshelf or a honey block. Bookshelves used to fetch far more.\n\n### 0.990.0\n\n**No more floating beds and villagers**\n\nVillages caught in one of the stranger stretches of the journey no longer leave beds and villagers hanging in mid-air beside the track.\n\n### 0.988.0\n\n**Farmer's Delight**\n\nFarmer's Delight isn't officially supported, but now it won't break the game at least.\n\n### 0.987.0\n\n**Faster creative sprint-flying**\n\nSprint-flying in creative is now 3\u00d7 faster by default. Normal flight and flying up or down are unchanged. Use /dt flyspeed 1 to go back to vanilla speed, or pick any multiplier you like.\n\n### 0.985.0\n\n**Some whitelisted mods need a recent Dungeon Train**\n\nA few mods on the whitelist are only approved on newer versions of Dungeon Train, because they rely on support those versions added. Run one on an older version and the run is Free Play until you update.\n\n- Update Dungeon Train to keep a mod like Catalogue on the whitelist\n\n### 0.984.0\n\n**The whitelist now covers settings changed mid-run**\n\nChanging a Dungeon Train balance setting while you're playing, whether in the settings screen or an in-game config editor, now puts that run into Free Play for good, just like using a tuning command. Changing it back before you quit no longer hides it.\n\n- How the train's mobs fight and scavenge now counts as a balance setting\n- So does whether your backpack survives death, and how big it can grow\n- The one-click settings reset puts these back to default along with everything else\n\n**Chat tells you when a new version drops**\n\nIf a new Dungeon Train version is released while you're playing, a line appears in chat saying which version is out and how long ago it dropped, with a link to what's new.\n\n- Only real releases are announced \u2014 never the small automatic ones\n- Turn it off in Options > Dungeon Train > New Version Chat",
    "0.983.0": "**Bug Fix \u00d71 \u00b7 Compatibility \u00d71**\n\n### 0.983.0\n\n**New worlds load again with ModernFix installed**\n\nStarting a new world with ModernFix installed \u2014 it ships in the modpack \u2014 could crash with \"Exception generating new chunk\", or leave the loading screen sitting at 33% for good. Both are fixed.\n\n- No change to how the world generates: the same seed still gives the same world, with ModernFix or without.",
    "0.982.0": "# Dimensions Overhaul 0.982.0\n\n## Number of dimensions\nA HUGE boost to the number of dimensions the train travels through. Many custom made for DT, some you may already know and love.\n\n## Shorter Dimensions\nDimensions are now short, pass through more quicker, but it will take longer to pass through them all.\n\n# The Whitelist for Mods\nMoving from blacklist to whitelist. Unless whitelisted, mods put you into freeplay. \nThe game will boot regardless, only whitelisted will enable high-scores.\n\n## Modpack Additions\n* **Advanced Shulkerboxes:** \n* **Sable Pathfinder:** *(Modrinth only for now)*\n* **Pigman Villagers:** ;)\n\n## Train Editor Tools\nThe train editor has undergone some big changes, make it work much better\n* **Test the Carriage** works on every carriage and contents template. Ctrl/Cmd+R re-rolls it\n* **Frames:** build your own to dress terrain dimensional carriages\n* **Doors, beds and tall plants** in block variants, with a new Span button\n* **Menus stay put** instead of following you, update as soon as you save, and no longer freeze on first open\n* **New** works for whole rooms and groups\n* **Save as new** on built-in templates, or keep a local edit\n* **Info panel** shows a build's lights and loot\n* **My Builds:** delete builds, and tell the reviewer about your build when you submit\n* Cmd/Ctrl-click deletes saved prefabs in the creative menu\n* Effortless Building breaks now clear block variants\n* Big shared builds keep their chest loot, and loading survives a busy server\n* Templates with thousands of block variants no longer lag\n\n## Bug Fixes\n* No more freezes when editing the train or saving\n* Distant Horizons no longer crashes on Mac\n* Dedicated servers now create Dungeon Train worlds\n* Eyes of ender lead to the same stronghold every time\n* Crops in dimensional carriages stay planted\n* Trees no longer turn the track into a tunnel\n\n## Bug fixes\n- New Biomes are cosmetics focused. New items and mobs on the train will be coming later."
  },
  "promos": {
    "1.21.1-latest": "0.1104.0",
    "1.21.1-recommended": "0.1104.0"
  }
}
